# Cloudflare Workers static-assets redirects (same syntax as Cloudflare Pages).
#
# Base64/Base32/Base58 were three separate tools, merged into one Base Converter
# tool (src/content/tools/base-encode-decode.mdx) so a visitor can switch formats
# without leaving the page. These are permanent (301) redirects, not a client-side
# trick, so Google consolidates each old page's ranking signal into the new URL
# instead of just hitting a 404. The ?format= query param deep-links straight into
# the matching format on load — see the ?format= handling in
# src/islands/BaseConverterTool.tsx.
/base64-encode-decode   /base-encode-decode/?format=base64   301
/base64-encode-decode/  /base-encode-decode/?format=base64   301
/base32-encode-decode   /base-encode-decode/?format=base32   301
/base32-encode-decode/  /base-encode-decode/?format=base32   301
/base58-encode-decode   /base-encode-decode/?format=base58   301
/base58-encode-decode/  /base-encode-decode/?format=base58   301

# There is no server-side search — the homepage has a client-side tool filter instead
# (src/lib/homeFilter.ts). Google still probes "/search?q=..." against most homepages
# looking for a Sitelinks Search Box, which was 404ing here. Cloudflare passes the
# incoming query string through to the destination by default, so ?q=test survives as
# /?q=test, and homeFilter.ts reads that on load to pre-fill and apply the filter.
/search   /   301
